Keep nvcc on stdexec's nonvirtual diagnostic fallback.

With stdexec commit 04de75de5807e73a229acf047c6976575e313359 and the other
nvcc patches applied, algorithm_sender_cuda.cu fails at __then.hpp:213 with
nvcc 12.8.93 and GCC 13.4.0: the then sender fails __well_formed_sender for
the unique_any_sender/transfer/bulk/then chain. Kokkos_Core.cpp and
Kokkos_Error.cpp fail the same constraint through HPX's host execution space.
Restoring only this guard makes the existing algorithm_sender_cuda regression
compile and pass with two host workers. It does not require a GPU.

Keep this separate so FetchContent checkouts with the GCC 13 patch already
applied can acquire it. The patch runner also accepts older checkouts where
the diagnostics guard was part of HPX_StdexecNvccGcc13.patch.

Tracking: https://github.com/TheHPXProject/hpx/pull/7711. Retest both
stdexec_cuda and algorithm_sender_cuda before removing this workaround.

